  "stem": "The matrix $\\mathbf{A} = \\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{pmatrix}$ has positive entries with $ad > bc$. By considering the image of the unit square, show that the area scale factor of the transformation is $ad - bc$.",
  "answerSpec": {
   "markScheme": {
    "points": [
     {
      "id": "p1",
      "description": "B1 the unit square $O(0,0)$, $(1,0)$, $(1,1)$, $(0,1)$ maps to the parallelogram $O$, $(a, c)$, $(a + b, c + d)$, $(b, d)$.",
      "marks": 1
     },
     {
      "id": "p2",
      "description": "M1 encloses the parallelogram in the rectangle $(a + b)$ by $(c + d)$.",
