      "marks": 1
     },
     {
      "id": "p4",
      "description": "A1 obtains $ad - bc$; since the unit square has area 1, every area is multiplied by $ad - bc$.",
      "marks": 1
     }
    ]
   },
   "modelAnswer": "The images of $\\mathbf{i}$ and $\\mathbf{j}$ are $(a, c)$ and $(b, d)$, so the unit square maps to the parallelogram with vertices $O$, $(a, c)$, $(a + b, c + d)$, $(b, d)$.\n$$\n\\text{Area} = (a + b)(c + d) - 2 \\cdot \\tfrac{1}{2}ac - 2 \\cdot \\tfrac{1}{2}bd - 2bc\n$$\n$$\n= ac + ad + bc + bd - ac - bd - 2bc = ad - bc\n$$\nThe unit square (area 1) becomes area $ad - bc = \\det\\mathbf{A}$; any shape is made of small squares, so all areas are multiplied by $\\det\\mathbf{A}$."
  },
